  "Question": "What is the units digit of \\(13^{2012}?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\( 1 \\)",
    "B": "\\( 3 \\)",
    "C": "\\( 5 \\)",
    "D": "\\( 7 \\)",
    "E": "\\( 9 \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "A product’s units digit depends only on the units digits of its factors, because every contribution from a higher place is a multiple of \\(10\\). Since \\(13\\) ends in \\(3\\), each successive power’s units digit comes from multiplying the previous units digit by \\(3\\).\n\nStarting with \\(13^1\\), the units digits are\n\\[\n3,\\ 9,\\ 7,\\ 1,\\ 3,\\ldots.\n\\]\nAfter \\(1\\), multiplying by \\(3\\) returns to \\(3\\), so the same four steps repeat. Since \\(2012=4\\cdot503\\), the requested power is at the end of a complete cycle. Its units digit is \\(\\boxed{1}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
